From: guillermo dieguez <dev@guillermodieguez.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:06:17 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix: check the iOS keyboard once the screen settles after a
 hide swipe

hideKeyboard swipes down a little and then polls the keyboard for up to two seconds before it tries a sideways swipe. On screens that do not dismiss the keyboard on a drag, every call spends those two seconds polling a keyboard that is not going anywhere.

The driver now waits for the screen to settle after the first swipe and checks the keyboard once. A keyboard that a drag dismisses is still moving until it is gone, so the screen only settles once it is hidden, and one that stays after the screen settles gets the sideways swipe right away.
---
 maestro-client/src/main/java/maestro/drivers/IOSDriver.kt | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/maestro-client/src/main/java/maestro/drivers/IOSDriver.kt b/maestro-client/src/main/java/maestro/drivers/IOSDriver.kt
index 6c0b290..152a1dd 100644
--- a/maestro-client/src/main/java/maestro/drivers/IOSDriver.kt
+++ b/maestro-client/src/main/java/maestro/drivers/IOSDriver.kt
@@ -396,7 +396,9 @@ class IOSDriver(
                 durationMs = 50,
             )
 
-            if (isKeyboardHidden(timeoutMs = 2000)) return@measured
+            waitForAppToSettle(null, null)
+
+            if (isKeyboardHidden()) return@measured
 
             swipe(
                 start = Point(0.5.asPercentOf(width), 0.5.asPercentOf(height)),
@@ -408,8 +410,7 @@ class IOSDriver(
         }
     }
 
-    private fun isKeyboardHidden(timeoutMs: Long = 0) =
-        MaestroTimer.withTimeout(timeoutMs) { if (isKeyboardVisible()) null else true } == true
+    private fun isKeyboardHidden() = !isKeyboardVisible()
 
     private fun dismissKeyboardIntroduction(heightPoints: Int) {
         val fastTypingInstruction =
